<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Titian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1488–<a href="/years/1576">1576</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Tiziano Vecellio</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Titian was the greatest painter of 16th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. His altarpieces such as the Assumption in the Frari, portraits and mythologies won him the patronage of popes, Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-spain">Philip II of Spain</a>. His mastery of colour and free brushwork shaped European painting for centuries. He died in Venice during a plague epidemic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/titian.jpg" alt="Titian" width="320" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Titian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Titian_-_Self-portrait_(Museo_del_Prado).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
